I made a Gaming Point Calculator to apply the Dart concepts I learned from our previous activities. I used classes and inheritance to organize the player information and make the code easier to understand. I also added a bonus point system that gives players extra points and determines their rank as Bronze, Silver, or Gold. I used an abstract class and a mixin to practice making my code more organized and reusable. I included async and await to simulate saving player information with a five-second delay. Through this activity, I learned how different Dart concepts can work together to create a simple gaming application.
